XHTTP server: a Push that waits for room in the upload queue no longer holds the lock Close needs

Upstream: f496437b84d4f05e07243da11fe380b302a82145

At the pin, uploadQueue.Push holds writeCloseMutex while it sends on pushedPackets, whose capacity is
scMaxBufferedPosts (30 by default), and Close takes the same mutex. A packet-up POST to a new session
id creates the session before any VLESS authentication and nothing reads its queue until a GET
arrives, so the 31st POST blocks inside Push, the session reaper's Close blocks behind it 30 seconds
later, and the session, its goroutines and its buffered payloads are never freed. Upstream #6372
(first in v26.6.27) drops the mutex: Push selects between the send and the queue's done.Instance,
Close closes that instance, the stream-up reader is published with an atomic compare-and-swap, and
Read selects on the same instance. The change in transport/internet/splithttp/upload_queue.go is
upstream's, without its comment; the file is identical at the pin and at the upstream commit's
parent. transport/internet/splithttp/upload_queue_close_test.go is fork code: it fills a queue of
30, starts a 31st Push and checks that Close returns and the waiting Push fails, and that packets
pushed out of order before any read still come out in sequence order.

